< https://github.com/tacplus-dev/kernel/issues/59#issuecomment-6890561317 https://github.com/tacplus-dev/kernel/issues/59
There was nothing new to land for #59: main already has everything this issue asks for. I've left the issue open as Jody decided, commented on it, and labelled it `needs-decision`.

- **Conflicts:** #48's batch commit 5ecc508 had already landed the same changes as this branch's c47cfd8. That covers the exception for the 8 CVEs, the decision record section with Jody's low risk rating (naming #47 and tacplus-dev/operator#30), and the PROPOSALS.md entries. I resolved all three files to main's version, so the branch now has no difference from main and there was nothing to commit.
- **Expiry date:** the exception expires 2026-12-14, not the 2026-12-13 Jody asked for here, because the #48 batch set that date. I pointed this out in the comment.
- **Security report:** the latest build scan of main shows 0 findings failing the policy. The 8 CVEs are accepted in all three jars that shade Hazelcast: `kernel.jar`, kernel-model's and codegen's.
- **Checks not run:** no build job, because there was no change to build. Rule 13 (trace propagation) didn't apply, since no handler changed. No patch release, because the real fix is the Hazelcast bump.
- **Still waiting:** the latest Hazelcast on Maven Central is still 5.7.0, so the bump can't happen yet.

**Decision needed:** this issue waits on an upstream Hazelcast release, not on another issue, so I can't record it as `Blocked-by:`. As long as it stays `approved` and unblocked, each new run will find nothing to do. My recommendation in the comment is to remove `approved` until a Hazelcast with patched Jackson ships, or until the 2026-12-14 expiry, whichever comes first.
